WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:05.430
Dave Springer:
My name is Dave Springer, graduate of 1984.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.160
I was a point guard, off guard.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.549
Played two years for Bill Morse and then my
last two years, junior and senior year, I

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:16.619
played for Coach Rod Halstead.

00:00:16.619 --> 00:00:23.189
I went to high school at Crestview High School
in Convoy, Ohio, and I really owe my opportunity

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.250
to come to Hillsdale to my high school coach,
Ray Etzler.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:31.910
I was a small town kid that had aspirations
to play college basketball and Coach Etzler

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:32.910
sent some letters out.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:38.120
Got an invite from the coach to come up here
for a visit and he said, "Throw in your gym

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.120
clothes."

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.250
I'll never forget the legendary athletic director
here, Jack McAvoy, who is a highly respected

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.250
man.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.310
He sent me down and he said, "Now, David,
as you go through this visit, they're going

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.550
to wine and dine and be really nice to you.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.390
Make sure you take the time to talk to some
people about Hillsdale."

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.170
I really learned a lot more about Hillsdale.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.340
Never regretted it.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.800
Personally, I feel I played on two of the
best teams that Hillsdale has ever had.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.080
My freshman year and senior year, I could
go on and on with a lot of guys.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:10.550
They're wonderful friends and they were wonderful
players.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:17.860
My freshman year, we were fourth in the nation,
so I was fortunate enough to be third team

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.400
All American, and I was player of the year
in the GLIAC.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.130
There is no way that would've happened without
those guys.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:28.830
If I'm not on two very successful teams, it
doesn't happen I'm not here talking to you

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:29.830
today.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:33.200
When you get my age, you learn not to take
anything for granted.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.180
I think you look back and how blessed you
were.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.850
Those are special, special times here at Hillsdale.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:42.610
The games were great and the basketball was
great, but it was more about sharing the ups

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:43.610
and downs.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:45.700
When you're in college, those are major decisions.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:48.500
Take a job, you're going to fall in love,
you're going to get married, whatever, but

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.030
you share those with your college friends.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:53.260
That means more to me than the basketball
part of it.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.710
Appreciated the opportunity, had a lot of
fun competing.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.880
Boy, the people part of it means more to me
now by far.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.680
I am very humbled and very touched by the
whole thing.

